msgid "Create a room"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Create a room on a StratiGraph node.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A room is a place on a node where a study lives and where the people of a"
" project work on it together. Whoever creates a room is its owner. A room"
" with one member is not a lesser room: it is your own table on the node, "
"and you can invite others to it later."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This page creates an **empty** room. To put the study you have open into "
"a new room, with its files, follow :doc:`bring-a-file-into-a-room` "
"instead: it creates the room in the same gesture."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Creating a room writes its owner on the node, so the node has to know who"
" you are. Three steps of the chip's menu at the top right must be done: "
"an **Author**, a **Node** that answers, and **Sign in** on it (see :doc"
":`sign-in`). If one is missing when you start, EMStudio opens that menu "
"at the missing step with a sentence such as «To create a room you need to"
" be signed in on the node: do it here and it goes on by itself», and the "
"creation resumes once the step is done."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create the room"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose ``File ▸ Create a room…``. The same command is **+ New room** in "
"the section **My space** of the chip's menu, under **Rooms on this "
"node**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dialog **Create a room** asks for a name, for example «Templu Mare "
"2026». EMStudio derives the room's identifier from the name, as the "
"node's own pages do: lower-case letters and digits, with hyphens in place"
" of spaces and punctuation (``templu-mare-2026``). A name made only of "
"punctuation gives no identifier, and the dialog waits for another one."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Press **Create** (or :kbd:`Enter`). **Cancel** (or :kbd:`Esc`) closes the"
" dialog without creating anything."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio asks the node that you are signed in on to create the room, and "
"enters it at once. On the web the node is the one that serves the page; "
"on the desktop it is the node you chose in the chip's menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the node refuses, a message gives its answer with its reason, for "
"example when a room with the same identifier already exists. If the node "
"does not answer, the message names it."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid "An empty room on the node, with you as its **owner**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The status bar reads **Room**, followed by the name of the room and of "
"the node, and the section **Where you work** of the chip's menu shows the"
" room with its commands."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The room appears under **Your rooms** in the section **My space**, and in"
" ``File ▸ Open Recent``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Next, invite the people of the project, as described in :doc:`enter-and-"
"share-a-room`."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`bring-a-file-into-a-room`, to create a room that holds your study."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`sign-in`, for the author, the node and the sign-in."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/explanation/open-enter-create`, on the three verbs: open a file, "
"enter a room, create a room."
msgstr ""

